  "body": "# [Experiment] E-B300-R01: cold GRU width versus depth at fixed training budget\n\n1. **Status, lineage and owner.** H-B300-R01 / E-B300-R01, labels-only student capacity branch; owned by SemyonEpanov's authorized tabdata campaign. This registers an already frozen and executing experiment, not a new prospective preregistration. Sixty strict-FP32 fits are planned. This is distinct from #2: near parameter counts and fixed updates, not matched measured FLOPs. Scientific source a266b036b02e8e012c6eb31072291dad618a169d; source-tree SHA256 `f4ef9ca8450a3e76d6b6f8295259e70aec5024d3a4f3296558bb0323add74130`. No teacher or pretrained initializer.\n\n2. **Why it should work.** A deeper recurrent composition may represent temporal interactions more efficiently than width alone. Predicted observation: deep-minus-wide gains across matched seeds and folds, rather than only one favorable fold. Additional optimization difficulty or unmatched arithmetic cost are competing explanations. This experiment estimates a fixed-recipe capacity contrast; it cannot establish a general depth scaling law.\n\n3. **Compute advantage.** Eight B300s provide 30 independent paired fitting cells per arm. Four measured concurrent actors per GPU share capacity with the separate PR15 experiment. Additional compute buys replication, not an assumed leaderboard gain. Serving cost and downstream distillation require separate evidence.\n\n4. **Frozen comparison.** Wide GRU H512x1 (2,210,306 parameters) versus deep H384x2 (2,151,554); wide is 2.73% larger. Input: 112 raw plus 99 canonical event features. Fit-only two-batch normalization, labels-only loss, batch8, context/chunk2000, six complete epochs, fixed epoch5 checkpoint. AdamW lr1e-4, beta2=.999, weight decay=.01, OneCycle warmup=.05, clipping1, dropout0. Strict FP32, autocast and TF32 disabled. Same fold/seed controls, no teacher, initialization warm start or automatic scientific retries. The frozen execution manifest is `95f82d442eefe425dde6574222b037ba1deba2d3ae36534aeec41e31e450874f`.\n\n5. **Thirty paired runs.** Per arm: F0/F1 seeds1003..1010, F2/F3 seeds1003..1009, an 8/8/7/7 matrix. Seeds1001/1002 remain externally owned and excluded. Panel SHA256 `471f465cc1d13fc6e5153a4c998390bb14e06823fed4c6721f929ce95fee47fb`; all sixty cells retain distinct fit claims. Resource profiles are excluded from replication counts.\n\n6. **Validation and significance.** Unchanged `global_wp_clip2_v1`, official target mask, component-qualified evaluation. Primary statistic: equal-fold mean of matched deep-minus-wide WP. Frozen 10,000 shared-fitting-seed bootstrap replicates, RNG271828; component uncertainty is evaluated separately. These are exposed development folds; fitting-seed intervals do not quantify selection or public-transfer uncertainty. Partial tables are descriptive and are not significance tests.\n\n7. **Leakage and coverage.** Frozen fold membership, fitting-only normalization and past-only recurrent inputs apply. No labels enter feature assembly. Source-qualified sequence/component identities must match fit/export/grade manifests; cross-fold evaluation is robustness evidence, not a pristine holdout. This capacity comparison does not establish representativeness for unobserved market regimes.\n\n8. **Decision-changing result.** Frozen decision SHA256 `32a9f0aaee4a0a839468c618853ec441d65e5bce91860a5b202454e931b235d7`. A useful absolute WP difference of .001 guides follow-up spending; it is not a universal significance threshold. Assess quality alongside measured runtime and serving cost. Preserve negative and inconclusive cells; a zero-crossing interval alone does not close the lineage. No automatic model promotion or leaderboard forecast.\n\n9. **How to run.** Existing deployment only: `/data/epanov_s/tabdata`, explicit `.venv/bin/python`, immutable `runtime/b300-r01-v1` and `runtime/source-a266-lf-subset-v1`. Active controller is `tabdata-r01-density4-v1`, using `runtime/r01-density4-v1/successor.py --authority receipts/r01-density4-admission-v1/AUTHORITY.json run`. Do not repeat that command while the service owns the panel. The original controller MainPID520360 is intentionally stopped; eight existing workers were adopted without restart. The successor retains the original absolute72h deadline and12h per-fit limit. Use `systemctl --user status tabdata-r01-density4-v1` to inspect, not a new controller. Separate reporter services never fit, export, grade or retry models.\n\n10. **Evidence to return.** Source/config/environment/ancestry, per-batch losses, LR, preclip gradient norms and step counts, original fit checkpoints, export manifests, prediction banks and official grade receipts. The reporter validates immutable chains before publication and creates separate evidence/weights archives plus SHA256 manifests under `/data/epanov_s/tabdata/artifacts/github-reporting-v1/`. Private data and weights are not uploaded to GitHub. Recovered PR15 exports preserve original failed receipts and missing original timing; they are not extra fits.\n\n11. **Results and trace.** [B300 campaign](../../campaign_2026-10-18/b300_execution_r1/README.md), [controller handoff](../../campaign_2026-10-18/b300_execution_r1/density4_v1/r01_successor/README.md), [reporter and authorization](../../campaign_2026-10-18/b300_execution_r1/github_reporting_v1/README.md). Before initial reporter deployment,32 scientific fits were active:16 R01 plus16 PR15;16 original PR15 endpoints were already scored. R01 official results are published only after receipt validation. Shared infrastructure and PR15 delivery repair in this branch are supporting evidence, not new R01 treatment arms. Per-endpoint comments retain failures, hashes and archive locations. Independent source/receipt reviews are recorded with the collectors; final CP30 inferential review remains required. No measured public-score claim.\n",
